WHY THE SOURCE IS PUBLIC

The repository is readable on purpose. The application was designed from the
outset to be maintainable by whoever holds the role next — with or without the
original author, and with or without a software background. Publishing the
source, the architecture notes, and the deployment steps is what makes that
true. It is published for reference and continuity, not for reuse.

